WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.465 --> 00:00:05.585
A beautiful café. Five stars. Hundreds of reviews. But three questions

2
00:00:05.585 --> 00:00:09.550
can still decide whether someone can visit. Can I get inside?

3
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.310
Reach a table? And use the toilet?

4
00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:19.043
For a wheelchair user, an unanswered detail can mean a wasted

5
00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:24.201
journey, an uncomfortable conversation, or a cancelled plan. The problem is

6
00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:28.438
not a lack of places. It is uncertainty before the journey.

7
00:00:30.464 --> 00:00:34.486
Venues face the other side of that uncertainty. People cannot choose

8
00:00:34.486 --> 00:00:39.436
confidently when practical details are missing. Staff repeat answers across calls

9
00:00:39.436 --> 00:00:44.600
and messages, while useful information stays disconnected from the next visitor.

10
00:00:45.464 --> 00:00:50.950
Meet AccessProof. A decision workspace that brings venue discovery, accessibility evidence,

11
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.424
and a direct question into one flow. Every feature has its

12
00:00:54.424 --> 00:00:59.600
own status. Missing information stays unknown. Conflicting reports stay visible.

13
00:01:00.463 --> 00:01:04.405
Start with real cafés in Indiranagar, Bengaluru. Serp A P I

14
00:01:04.405 --> 00:01:10.047
retrieves venue listings and explicit accessibility attributes. Compare entrances, seating, and

15
00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:13.746
toilets side by side. A high rating never becomes an accessibility

16
00:01:13.746 --> 00:01:14.600
claim.

17
00:01:15.464 --> 00:01:18.686
When a detail is missing, the research agent uses Tavily to

18
00:01:18.686 --> 00:01:23.482
check public sources. It assesses venue and locality matches, and adapts

19
00:01:23.482 --> 00:01:27.158
its query if the first check is insufficient. The budget is

20
00:01:27.158 --> 00:01:29.600
bounded: at most two searches.

21
00:01:30.464 --> 00:01:34.545
The agent drafts a specific question, then stops for your review.

22
00:01:34.545 --> 00:01:38.141
It is an explainable policy agent, without a large language model

23
00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:42.832
planner. Search clues never update the accessibility table. You control the

24
00:01:42.832 --> 00:01:44.600
question and invitation.

25
00:01:45.464 --> 00:01:49.295
Now watch the moment that matters. This venue is fictional, but

26
00:01:49.295 --> 00:01:54.175
the Nexconn delivery is real. The representative answers the toilet question.

27
00:01:54.175 --> 00:01:58.224
The visitor's table changes from unknown to reported available, with author

28
00:01:58.224 --> 00:01:59.600
and time.

29
00:02:00.463 --> 00:02:03.865
Open the evidence and inspect what was said. An unsure answer

30
00:02:03.865 --> 00:02:08.194
leaves the question unresolved. An opposing report creates a conflict. A

31
00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:12.365
representative report is an attributed claim, not an independent inspection or

32
00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.600
an accessibility certificate.

33
00:02:15.463 --> 00:02:19.495
Our business hypothesis is simple. Free discovery for visitors, and paid

34
00:02:19.495 --> 00:02:24.433
enquiry management and profile maintenance for venues and hospitality groups. Next,

35
00:02:24.433 --> 00:02:28.510
we would test staff response rates, visitor decision usefulness, and willingness

36
00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.600
to pay.

37
00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:35.398
The working prototype connects Tavily research, private Nexconn chat, and persistent

38
00:02:35.398 --> 00:02:40.786
evidence on Cloud Run. Twenty seven automated tests passed. Real research

39
00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:43.454
and the live reply to table flow were tested end to

40
00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:44.600
end.

41
00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:49.673
AccessProof turns an information gap into a question someone can answer,

42
00:02:49.673 --> 00:02:53.317
and keeps that answer attached to the decision. Because a great

43
00:02:53.317 --> 00:02:58.405
outing should begin with clearer plans. AccessProof. Find the evidence. Ask

44
00:02:58.405 --> 00:02:59.600
what is missing.
